-aware unified pre-trained encoder-decoder models for code understanding and generation\n\t\t\n\t\t\tYueWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWeishiWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tRShafiq\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tStevenC HJoty\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHoi\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tEMNLP\n\t\t\n\t\t\tAssociation for Computational Linguistics\n\t\t\t2021","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Codet5: Identifier-aware unified pre-trained encoder-decoder models for code understanding and generation"},{"raw_text":"Emergent abilities of large language models\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJasonWei\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tYiTay\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tRishiBommasani\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tColinRaffel\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tBarretZoph\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSebastianBorgeaud\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDaniYogatama\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMaartenBosma\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDennyZhou\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDonaldMetzler\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tEdHChi\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTatsunoriHashimoto\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOriolVinyals\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPercyLiang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJeffDean\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWilliamFedus\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2022\n\t\t\n\t\n\tSurvey Certification","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Emergent abilities of large language models"},{"raw_text":"Chain-of-thought prompting elicits reasoning in large language models\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJasonWei\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tXuezhiWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDaleSchuurmans\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMaartenBosma\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tBrianIchter\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFeiXia\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tEdChi\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tQuocLe\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDennyZhou\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2201.11903\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2023\n\t\t\n\t\n\tPreprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2201.11903","title":null},{"raw_text":"Executing the code on the test input gives {&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Blue&apos;, &apos;P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;, &apos;G&apos;: &apos;Green&apos;, &apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;, &apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;}, the same as the LLM&apos;s reasoning with Imagined Execution. Indeed, the LLM&apos;s reasoning is correct: the executed result and the expected result are not the same, where B should be mapped to Black instead of Blue. The synthesized code does not map the B key correctly, thus the synthesized code is wrong\n\t\t\n\t\t\tShunyuYao\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDianYu\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJeffreyZhao\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tIzhakShafran\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTomGriffiths\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tYuanCao\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKarthikNarasimhan\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2024\n\t\t\t36\n\t\t\n\t\n\tTree of thoughts: Deliberate problem solving with large language models B&apos;: &apos;Black P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;}, {&apos;G&apos;: &apos; Green&apos;, &apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;}, {&apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Blue&apos;}) == ? Answer in &lt;test_case&gt; Given the reasoning above, complete the following test case. assert merge_dictionaries_three({&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red P&apos;: &apos;Pink G&apos;: &apos;Green W&apos;: &apos;White &lt;/test_case&gt; tag. Output: assert merge_dictionaries_three({&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Black&apos;, &apos;P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;}, {&apos;G&apos;: &apos; Green&apos;, &apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;}, {&apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Blue&apos;}) == {&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos; Blue L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;} The canonical test case is &quot;assert merge_dictionaries_three({&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Black&apos;, &apos;P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;}, {&apos;G&apos;: &apos;Green&apos;, &apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;}, {&apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Blue&apos;}) == {&apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;, &apos;P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Black&apos;, &apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;G&apos;: &apos;Green&apos;, &apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;} and our Code Quality Checker correctly rejects this code. Note that the LLM has explained the mapping of B key explicitly, showing the strength of our Imagined Execution method in predicting synthesized code correctness","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Executing the code on the test input gives {&apos;R&apos;: &apos;Red&apos;, &apos;B&apos;: &apos;Blue&apos;, &apos;P&apos;: &apos;Pink&apos;, &apos;G&apos;: &apos;Green&apos;, &apos;W&apos;: &apos;White&apos;, &apos;L&apos;: &apos;lavender&apos;}, the same as the LLM&apos;s reasoning with Imagined Execution. Indeed, the LLM&apos;s reasoning is correct: the executed result and the expected result are not the same, where B should be mapped to Black instead of Blue. The synthesized code does not map the B key correctly, thus the synthesized code is wrong"}],"layout_json":null,"tei_xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<TEI xml:space=\"preserve\" xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" \nxmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" \nxsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kermitt2/grobid/master/grobid-home/schemas/xsd/Grobid.xsd\"\n xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\t<teiHeader xml:lang=\"en\">\n\t\t<fileDesc>\n\t\t\t<titleStmt>\n\t\t\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">QualityFlow: An Agentic Workflow for Program Synthesis Controlled by LLM Quality Checks</title>\n\t\t\t</titleStmt>\n\t\t\t<publicationStmt>\n\t\t\t\t<publisher/>\n\t\t\t\t<availability  status=\"unknown\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<licence/>\n\t\t\t\t</availability>\n\t\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2025-03-24\">24 Mar 2025</date>\n\t\t\t</publicationStmt>\n\t\t\t<sourceDesc>\n\t\t\t\t<biblStruct status=\"extracted\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<analytic>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Yaojie</forename><surname>Hu</surname></persName>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<affiliation key=\"aff0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"institution\" key=\"instit1\">Iowa State University</orgName>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"instituti